ADDITIONAL NOTICE — AUTHORISED USE ONLY

wafharness models how request parsers interpret bytes. It sends no traffic by
itself. Any requests you build from its output must target only systems for
which you hold explicit, documented authorisation: an engagement contract, a bug
bounty program scope that permits the activity, or systems you own.

Testing a WAF outside an authorised scope can violate computer-misuse law in
most jurisdictions and the terms of the program you are working under. The
authors accept no liability for misuse.
